> Try adding whiskey and/or vanilla essence.

Heat the oven to 210°C.

> Try a higher temperature next time: it took 1 hour 20 minutes to cook at 210°C, and did not end up particularly deep brown on top.

Grease and line a #deep 20 cm cake tin{} with baking paper, so it comes up at least 2 cm above the top of the rim. Lay in a second sheet of paper at right angles, and weigh down the paper with a bowl if needed.

Put the @cream cheese{700%g}(at room temperature) in a large bowl, food processor, or food mixer. Beat on a low speed until soft and spreadable.

Beat in the @crème fraîche{350%g}(at room temperature) until evenly mixed in. Add the @caster sugar{300%g} and @salt{0.5%tsp}, and beat until dissolved.

Beat in the @eggs{5}(beaten) one by one, scraping down the walls of the bowl, until they are thoroughly mixed in.

Put the @cornflour{2%tbsp} in a small bowl, whisk to break up any lumps, then beat in a spoonful of the batter until thoroughly mixed in. Pour the cornflour mix into the big bowl of batter and stir to combine.

Pour the cake mix into the lined tin. Smooth the top, then pick up the tin and drop it a couple of times on a work surface to knock out any air bubbles.

Bake for 30 to ~{45%minutes}, until the top is deeply brown but the middle is still wobbly and liquid (it will set as it cools). The internal temperature should be at least 60°C.

Remove from the oven and leave to cool, before using the paper to help lift the cake out of its tin. Either serve whilst still warm, or refrigerate for several hours so that it can be cut neatly.